    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. one thing though—for the natural stone, how bad is the damage from accidental scratches or if someone spills something acidic? like, is it something that happens gradually or is it more sudden? also, if we go with concrete, does it show every little scuff or mark pretty easily?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Acid spills on natural stone are a serious concern, as they can cause immediate, localized etching—it's not a gradual wear, but a sudden chemical attack that dulls the surface finish. For the stone, the severity depends on the stone type and the acid, but a strong spill can leave a permanent mark. With concrete, the visibility of scuffs is highly dependent on the finish and the color chosen. A very dark, highly polished concrete might hide minor scuffs better, but any significant abrasion or deep gouge will be quite noticeable, much like a very large, poorly-placed piece of gravel on a path.",
